{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for the complete Stage 5 scope, original a5d64b35e87c97560ff354578d9560bd1261aacb / builder d5378da5583d3bc16c0c19094c1d4c8716aceb2b, at exact 736f4953a50b67f7d1fc0c5f4e96dfb9ee02f2b7. Primary 06d9af263106d20f75d9edcc4e5b075f7ffbb49a is first, with all 111 submitted artifacts. Each is individually effective with direct sole builder-promise provenance; I independently recomputed every exact Git blob, byte count and SHA256: 9,310,539 bytes, including 16 binary PNGs, no mismatch. The path set is unchanged from 048c; 107 artifacts are byte-identical, with only client room.ts, prepared.test.ts and the two plan files changed. Source succession notices are metadata limits, not proof of runtime behavior. The fresh invitation and own promise a2615d3b preserve Stage 5's assigned scope without overriding a retired basis or silently adding the original MCP contract review.\n\nThe accessor repair b2043423 is supported. plainCopy at client room.ts165–195 checks each owned property descriptor and copies that same value once. An enumerable getter is refused without invocation, and a class instance is refused before prototype erasure. The shipped fourteen-value table and independent original changing-getter witness both pass: 2 executed, 10 unselected, exit 0, 0.439s. The private witness checks direct-class refusal and ordinary legal-data success, actual local Ed25519 signature validity and the literal HTTP body. Getter reads, additional act signatures, preparation hooks and POSTs are all zero. One isolated relaxation of the descriptor guard makes both same loaded witnesses fail by AssertionError: 0 passed, 2 failed, exit 1, 0.388s. Root verified all 12 exact source/fixture identities, two probe/config identities and 15 saved evidence hashes; the controlled source is restored. This is exact client code over the unchanged FakeRoom HTTPS seam, not a real Room/provider test. Evidence: /tmp/artroom-checker-stage5-736f-b4vxzw1m. It closes the demonstrated validation/copy disagreement; it does not resolve the following independent findings.\n\n1. P2 — Reserve unresolved-act capacity before awaiting (client room.ts388–416; durable f7740b54909a52e192704a89689278b6b5ef0829). The entire named-method implementation is byte-identical to 048c, independently compared. The 048c actual witness seeded 63 accepted/lost replies and released two new calls together. Both passed the same available slot, signed, called onPrepared, POSTed and were accepted with lost replies: 65 retained instead of 64. The loaded bound assertion fails, 0 passed / 1 failed, exit 1; the shipped serial witness passes. Oldest and both concurrent keys still settle after activation with original receipts, identical prepared canonical bytes and captured literal HTTP bodies, no fresh signatures or effects. Eviction 6bf8d38a stays repaired; concurrent backpressure does not. Reserve before the first await, release for known settlement or never-dispatched work, retain for uncertain dispatch. Preserve both the bound and original bytes. Root previously vetted the full probe and 15 source/fixture plus two probe/config hashes; the exact named-method equality transfers that evidence, without a new 736f run. Evidence: /tmp/artroom-checker-stage5-048c-cwox6gjb. Seam: exact client and actual synthetic signer over FakeRoom; no real Room/provider credit.\n\n2. P2 — Preserve unresolved UI intent across catalogue presentation changes (Acts.tsx182,209,392–443; LiveRoom143–169; durable 4a1387040825fbff66bd4e3bc8e11a6dfd1c2a69). The full UI tree is unchanged; root independently checked nine relevant exact identities. The prior actual ActsScreen/LiveRoom witness over MemoryRoom in happy-dom shows accepted/lost reply uncertainty and exact settlement. An ordinary catalogue read failure returns null and unmounts the form child that owns the saved intent. Restoring the identical catalogue on the same open page gives a blank fresh form, loses uncertainty and same-act retry, and accepts a fresh-key act before the first is settled. The no-null control settles the original same key/body/binding with one effect. This proves premature fresh-intent availability, not an automatic duplicate of the same body. Keep intent/status ownership above presentation gates until the outcome is known or the user deliberately chooses Leave it, while displaying catalogue unavailability honestly. The corrected focused probe has one loaded AssertionError, exit 1; its initial harness mistake/incidental broad diagnostic run remains explicitly excluded from gate credit. Root previously vetted the actual probe and eleven source/probe/config hashes. No new UI run is claimed at 736f. Evidence: /tmp/artroom-checker-stage5-c38-eviction-st4tv4kb. No production browser, actual Room signatures or provider credit.\n\n3. Original authenticated UI entry remains owed. Original condition 1 requires preparing/submitting an application act in the normal authenticated declaration surface; condition 3 requires showing the actual unknown act in CLI/UI. The generic form and LiveRoom adapter exist, but main.tsx25–31 still selects only MemoryRoom declared demo or MockRoom. No authenticated entry reaches the Room. Original a5, fa120186's preservation of complete scope, ratified 41a5a2b4's ordering-only amendment and adopted design sections 8.1/8.5 contain no mock-only final-delivery exception. Complete that integration with an actual witness through existing client/credential/surface owners, or obtain an explicit requester scope decision. This finding prescribes no new OAuth/login/room-selection design, deployment, duplicate commission or first-Jam gate.\n\nThe earlier client/CLI repairs remain supported by their historical exact-source evidence, including unsupported plain-data refusal and the journal's distinction between a sent replay and an already held answer. Prior repaired findings are not relabelled as fresh runtime proofs. Authenticated catalogue reads, explicit generic bindings, finite signed grant maps, retained D(s) readers and shared declaration/rendering helpers otherwise remain coherent. No authority expansion was found in the getter delta.\n\nArchitecture: owned snapshots, unresolved capacity and pending intent must survive ordinary asynchronous dispatch and presentation changes. The one-pass copy repairs one boundary; reservation and UI ownership remain necessary. Security: current permission and explicit binding govern admission; a loss of outcome cannot authorize silently replacing intent. Simplification: use one checked copy, one capacity reservation lifecycle and one pending-intent owner, preserving bounded retention and deliberate settlement.\n\nThe clean exact checkout passes git diff --check for the complete delta. Builder's reported 2,031-test gate and control are recorded evidence; this review did not rerun the broad gate/browser suite. The inherited core is byte-identical to separately approved Stage 2 at 39430e23 (9cb05da9); withdrawn 25bede37 remains withdrawn. Correct the current Stage 5 report's old approval reference and qualify its maximum-64 claim until concurrent reservation is repaired. The invariant-map deletion of the retired-grantor bearer gap at 736f gives no bearer repair credit here: requests.ts remains the older source at this head. The later 87cd5804/5d41 bearer repair has its own six-artifact review.\n\nStage 3 full accounting/whole-log negative, Stage 4 mapping, authenticated UI entry, MCP runtime and original contract dual binding retain their own obligations. Historical 048c planner contract publications are read evidence, not final MCP composition approval. Stage 5's assigned review does not implicitly close a978/ee3 or 9ca/bac. Full functionality and final exact-head composition checks remain; estimates only sequence the work. Complete identity inventory: /tmp/artroom-s5-736f-identity-ofv58nh1.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:06d9af263106d20f75d9ed